# servants_thine: in P3 and A2, "counted in thy possessions" means ownership, in line with S3's "really thine". In A5, vicious servants are excluded because they are a harm, not because they belong to someone else; that reading is about worth. A2 then carries only the ownership sense to C.
# No single premise or assumption joins the two senses of one word, so I name no bridge. The shift happens across the separate uses of servants_thine.
# beauty_thine: "what is that to thee" is read as "of no concern or value to thee" in A3, C1 and A4 alike, so I count it as one sense.
